# Vercel auto-installs a requirements.txt found at the project root as a
# generic pre-build step, independent of vercel.json/buildCommand. The
# repo root's requirements.txt belongs to the PySide6 desktop app
# (pyside6-essentials, pyside6-addons, numpy, pandas, matplotlib...) and
# has nothing to do with the web deployment - installing it blew the
# Python function bundle past the 500MB limit. This is the only line
# that's actually needed to fix that; it's kept minimal on purpose after
# a broader version of this file (excluding main.py, config.py, etc. by
# bare name) turned out to also match and exclude api/app/main.py,
# api/app/config.py, and api/requirements.txt, since unanchored
# gitignore-style patterns match at any depth, not just the root.
/requirements.txt
